    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d442-a1">

                <pb facs="0468" n="1202" xml:id="pg1202"/>

                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Inclosure in No. 34.]</seg></opener>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">District Attorney Aycock to
                        the Attorney-General</hi>.</head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Telegram.]</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington, N. C</hi></placeName>., <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1895-09-20"><hi rendition="#italic">September 20,
                        1895</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p>Have libeled steamer <hi rendition="#italic">Commodore</hi> and cargo, under
                    section <hi rendition="#italic">5283</hi>, and have had arrested for violation
                    of section 5286 John G. Dillon, master; George H. Martin, first officer; Frank
                    p. Grain, second officer; Manuel Hendio, cook; John B. Vanivie, chief engineer;
                    and Mark Reilley, assistant engineer. Can you furnish any evidence in regard to
                    the shipment of arms and ammunition or the connection of Charles Raymond or any
                    of above parties with same?</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">C. B. Aycock</hi>,<lb/><hi
                            rendition="#italic">United States Attorney.</hi></signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
